# NOTICE

## Third-party protocol reference

The WeChat iLink Bot API wire protocol implemented in `src/ilink/` was written
against the publicly documented behavior of Tencent's official WeChat channel
plugin:

- **Package:** `@tencent-weixin/openclaw-weixin`
- **Copyright:** © Tencent
- **License:** MIT
- **Reference version:** 2.4.9

The implementation here is an independent TypeScript implementation targeting
DeepSeek Harness 0.2.0-rc.2. No source code from that package is vendored or
copied; the protocol layer was written from its documented request/response
contracts (endpoints, headers, message shapes, error codes, and CDN
encryption rules).

Documented protocol facts used:

- Endpoints: `ilink/bot/get_bot_qrcode`, `get_qrcode_status`, `getupdates`,
  `sendmessage`, `getconfig`, `sendtyping`, `getuploadurl`
- Base URL `https://ilinkai.weixin.qq.com`, CDN `https://novac2c.cdn.weixin.qq.com/c2c`
- Headers: `iLink-App-Id`, `iLink-App-ClientVersion`, `AuthorizationType`,
  `Authorization`, `X-WECHAT-UIN`, optional `SKRouteTag`
- `X-WECHAT-UIN` = base64(decimal string of a random uint32)
- Error code `-14` = session expired (requires QR re-login)
- Media encryption: AES-128-ECB with PKCS7; `aes_key` appears in two encodings
  (base64 of raw 16 bytes, and base64 of the 32-char hex string)

## Dependencies

- `qrcode-terminal` — MIT — renders the login QR code in a terminal.

## Node.js

This package targets Node.js ≥ 22.13.0 and uses only built-in modules plus the
dependency above.
